{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/noteheadText-swift.property"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"noteheadText","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"noteheadText"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV12NoteheadTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoteheadText"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV12noteheadTextAC08NoteheadE0VSgvp","symbolKind":"property"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/noteheadtext-swift.property"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The text displayed inside the notehead, if any."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"noteheadText"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV12NoteheadTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoteheadText","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/NoteheadText-swift.struct"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<notehead-text>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/noteheadText-swift.property":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The text displayed inside the notehead, if any."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/noteheadtext-swift.property","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"noteheadText","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoteheadText","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV12NoteheadTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"noteheadText","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/noteheadText-swift.property"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNote","abstract":[{"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/NoteheadText-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLNote.NoteheadText","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/NoteheadText-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The notehead-text type represents text that is displayed inside a notehead, as is done in some educational"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"music. It is not needed for the numbers used in tablature or jianpu notation. The presence of a TAB or jianpu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clefs is sufficient to indicate that numbers are used. The display-text and accidental-text elements allow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display of fully formatted text and accidentals."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoteheadText"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoteheadText"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/noteheadtext-swift.struct"}}}